### 1. Admin signin (expect 200 + token, role admin)
# @name adminSignin
POST http://localhost:3000/auth/signin
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "salshafi44m@gmail.com", "password": "YOUR_ADMIN_PASSWORD"}

### 2. Create project with NO token (expect 401)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/projects
Content-Type: application/json

{"title": "Test", "description": "Test"}

### 3. Create project with ADMIN token (expect 201)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/projects
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminSignin.response.body.token}}

{
  "title": "Admin Test Project",
  "firstname": "Salman",
  "lastname": "Shafi",
  "email": "sal@example.com",
  "completion": "2026-10-01",
  "description": "Created by admin"
}

### 4a. Signup a normal user (expect 201)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Test User", "email": "user@test.com", "password": "test1234"}

### 4b. Normal user signin
# @name usersignin
POST http://localhost:3000/auth/signin
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "user@test.com", "password": "test1234"}

### 4c. Create project as NORMAL user (expect 403)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/projects
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{usersignin.response.body.token}}

{
  "title": "Normal User Project",
  "firstname": "Test",
  "lastname": "User",
  "email": "user@test.com",
  "completion": "2026-10-01",
  "description": "Should be blocked"
}

### 5. Anyone can read projects (expect 200)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/projects

### Sign out (clears the cookie)
GET http://localhost:3000/auth/signout